{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00321",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 2.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Hi. Thanks for coming in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.03,
      "end_seconds": 4.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.87,
      "end_seconds": 8.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "How can I help you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.56,
      "end_seconds": 21.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "It's a fever that won't go away, mostly. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.28,
      "end_seconds": 24.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.36,
      "end_seconds": 29.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "It's been one week now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.93,
      "end_seconds": 33.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.59,
      "end_seconds": 43.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "It happens once or twice a day. Uh, and I've been feeling weak as well, for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.16,
      "end_seconds": 44.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.93,
      "end_seconds": 52.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "I did have a dull stomach ache at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.92,
      "end_seconds": 57.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Alright, I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.37,
      "end_seconds": 59.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.72,
      "end_seconds": 78.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Any vomiting, jaundice or burning when passing urine at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.2,
      "end_seconds": 86.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Um, you know, no vomiting, jaundice or burning when passing urine, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.86,
      "end_seconds": 91.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Alright, moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.08,
      "end_seconds": 102.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for two years now. It's the not knowing that gets to me. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.86,
      "end_seconds": 111.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "Right. Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.97,
      "end_seconds": 115.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "I, I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.39,
      "end_seconds": 120.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.73,
      "end_seconds": 124.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Yes, pollen, it gives me a runny nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.36,
      "end_seconds": 128.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.33,
      "end_seconds": 142.43,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.39,
      "end_seconds": 144.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.01,
      "end_seconds": 150.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.1,
      "end_seconds": 156.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.53,
      "end_seconds": 160.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Glycomet, 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.84,
      "end_seconds": 165.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.0,
      "end_seconds": 167.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.47,
      "end_seconds": 172.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.63,
      "end_seconds": 177.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Yes, uh, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.69,
      "end_seconds": 183.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.65,
      "end_seconds": 191.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.01,
      "end_seconds": 217.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 107, weight 75 kilos, saturation 98 percent, blood pressure 123 over 76, height 151 centimetres, BMI works out to 32.9. Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.26,
      "end_seconds": 221.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Right, no problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.78,
      "end_seconds": 223.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.26,
      "end_seconds": 234.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "Yeah, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.14,
      "end_seconds": 259.21,
      "duration_seconds": 23.07,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: This looks most like typhoid fever, which we need to confirm. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep malaria in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a fever that won't go away for one week, and no jaundice or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.34,
      "end_seconds": 263.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.77,
      "end_seconds": 268.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just typing this up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.75,
      "end_seconds": 293.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Okay, continuing. Let's get blood cultures, for prolonged fever. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 293.72,
      "end_seconds": 297.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I can book that for Wednesday at 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.06,
      "end_seconds": 300.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Wednesday, that works for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.16,
      "end_seconds": 308.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "I'm prescribing paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for fever and body aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.75,
      "end_seconds": 312.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Oh, okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.15,
      "end_seconds": 341.18,
      "duration_seconds": 27.03,
      "text": "Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.54,
      "end_seconds": 343.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.42,
      "end_seconds": 361.02,
      "duration_seconds": 17.6,
      "text": "If the fever stays high or the tummy pain gets sharp, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Come back in three days. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.75,
      "end_seconds": 375.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed and come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.09,
      "end_seconds": 381.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.33,
      "end_seconds": 387.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "No, you know, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}